    "user_prompt": "Build an 8-bit valid-ready stream fork datapath as a complete SR2FPGA Verilog RTL project. This is component topology t3_stream_fork, difficulty tier T3. Use a skid_buffer feeding a stream_fork and two stream_stage outputs. The design must implement this black-box behavior: valid input samples pass through a skid buffer and are duplicated to two output stages. Keep rtl/top.v as the integration wrapper and keep each reusable component in a separate RTL file. Preserve these interface contracts: top.in_valid -> skid_buffer.in_valid; top.in_data -> skid_buffer.in_data; skid_buffer.out_valid -> stream_fork.in_valid; skid_buffer.out_data -> stream_fork.in_data; stream_fork.in_ready -> skid_buffer.out_ready; stream_fork.out0_valid -> stream_stage.in_valid; stream_fork.out0_data -> stream_stage.in_data; stream_stage.in_ready -> stream_fork.out0_ready; stream_fork.out1_valid -> stream_stage.in_valid; stream_fork.out1_data -> stream_stage.in_data; stream_stage.in_ready -> stream_fork.out1_ready; stream_stage.out_valid -> top.out0_valid; stream_stage.out_data -> top.out0_data; stream_stage.out_valid -> top.out1_valid; stream_stage.out_data -> top.out1_data. Include system_his.json, manifest.json, timing constraints, predicted QoR, and a bounded self-checking testbench that prints TEST_PASS only on success or TEST_FAIL on failure.",
    "design_goal": "Implement an 8-bit valid-ready stream fork with skid buffer input stage and two registered output stages, suitable for generic FPGA synthesis.",
    "assumptions": [
      "Clock frequency 100 MHz",
      "Active-low asynchronous reset",
      "Data width is 8 bits",
      "Valid-ready handshake protocol on all stream interfaces",
      "Skid buffer provides one pipeline stage to improve timing on input",
      "Stream fork duplicates input stream to two outputs, gated by both output ready signals",
      "Stream stages each provide one register on data and valid signals",
      "All components share the same clock and reset domain"
    ]
